Z||000000||JohnnyK||04-12-2001||09:16 PM||||I don't freaking get this. New line, and the master and slave don't seem to be leaking, and it's working fine, but I notice the engage point becoming lower and lower (this is throughout the course of an hour maybe) and then, within about 3 stoplights, it loses a LOT of pressure, and it basically flops halfway down to the floor. So much that I had to stop it to get in gear, so we played th game of driving across the city, using parking lots and such so that we wouldn't have to come to a stop. IT DOESN"T MAKE SENSE! And then after I stopped for a sec, the pressure seemed to come back for a minute, and then it was gone again!!! All the fluid is still there though!||||reg||8
Z||000001||fiero56||04-12-2001||09:21 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by JohnnyK:<BR><B>I don't freaking get this. New line, and the master and slave don't seem to be leaking, </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Don't seem to be leaking...they are the only thing left, just replace them and you won't have to mess with this anymore. Just remember buy GM master and slave.||||reg||1
