Z||000005||fiero56||04-13-2001||09:07 AM||||<P>You own a car, it has a problem. This particular problem is causing your car to be undriveable(and unsafe the way I see it). You know what the problem is, yet you continue to post the same problem here, surprised when hear the same solution time after time. Ignoring it isn't going to make it go away.<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 04-13-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||Wade87GT||04-13-2001||09:37 AM||||If you're using any of those rebuilt lifetime warranty M/C or Slaves, they are prone to sudden failure. Replace both with new GM parts (otherwise one will contaminate the new part). I went through several, some were bad out of the box, until I did it the right way. Don't forget to purge the clutch line. I purged mine with new fluid, that cleaned out the debris and got out the air bubbles at the same time. Cap off the ends right away with those little rubber vacuum caps. This will keep out the dirt and air until you're ready to hook them up to the cylinders.<P>Wade<p>[This message has been edited by Wade87GT (edited 04-13-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||JohnnyK||04-13-2001||01:42 PM||||Fiero56: Perhaps you an I see things in a different light. I don't see HOW this is an "unsafe" vehicle because the clutch isn't disengaging all the way.. Uh oh, perhaps I have to make a sudden stop, and I stall the car.. Or worse, I can't get it back into gear!!! Whats the worst that is going to happen. A semi is going to be barelling a long, and I won't be able to jump out of the way in time (it's a 4cyl Fiero, i wouldn't be able to DRIVE out of the way in time). What i want to know is what this problem with the master cylinder is, and someone said you can fix it with a washer. I would like to try that BEFORE I am forced to buy a new master and slave. After all, i had the slave out a few months ago, dismantled and inspected, and it looked fine.||||reg||1
